From: Korri <korri@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: sun50i-h616: decode without the IOMMU

Korri experiment, not upstream. With the VE on the IOMMU, Linux turns on
translation for every master and the display engine faults on wake
(docs/research/h700-video-engine-worksheet.md). The H6-class VE accepts
physical addresses: before the H6 IOMMU driver existed, its Cedrus variant
set CEDRUS_QUIRK_NO_DMA_OFFSET and decoded from CMA (Linux v5.4). Give the
VE its own reusable CMA pool and no IOMMU link, so nothing attaches to the
IOMMU and the display path stays as it is without the VE.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -117,6 +117,20 @@
 			reg = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x40000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * Korri: the video engine allocates from this pool and uses
+		 * physical addresses, so the IOMMU stays off and the display
+		 * engine's DMA is unchanged. Reusable: the kernel lends the
+		 * pages to movable allocations while the decoder is idle.
+		 */
+		ve_pool: ve-pool {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			reusable;
+			size = <0x0 0x4000000>;
+			alignment = <0x0 0x2000>;
+			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x40000000>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	osc24M: osc24M-clk {
@@ -266,8 +280,8 @@
 			clock-names = "ahb", "mod", "ram";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_VE>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 93 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-			iommus = <&iommu 3>, <&iommu 2>;
 			allwinner,sram = <&ve_sram 1>, <&sram_c 1>;
+			memory-region = <&ve_pool>;
 		};
 
 		syscon: syscon@3000000 {
